# Review ownership.
#
# This file used to encode the parallel-work arrangement from docs/PLAN.md §7 —
# one team per workstream, disjoint file ownership, so a pull request touching
# someone else's paths was flagged here rather than discovered in a rebase. That
# arrangement did its job and the workstreams have merged; the matrix is still
# in PLAN.md §7 for anyone reading the history.
#
# What it cannot be is a list of teams that do not exist. GitHub silently
# ignores a rule naming a team it cannot resolve, so a CODEOWNERS full of them
# looks like review protection while providing none — which is worse than
# having no file at all. Every one of the ws-* handles it named was unresolvable.
#
# So: one owner, who exists.

* @AbyssinianGuy
